<title>SPAIN: Santander cuts prime rate to 7.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Santander cuts prime rate to 7.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Banco Santander said on Friday it cut its prime rate to 7.5 percent from 7.75 percent.</p>
<p>Earlier, the central bank cut its key money market rate to 5.75 percent from six percent, its second reduction this year.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
